diff --git a/docs/browser-performance.md b/docs/browser-performance.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1fc2a3f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/browser-performance.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Browser performance and guest panic investigation
+
+The supplied 88875251 henge.log is build 0580d855 (before the native Metal display
+shader revision), four CPUs, 14 GiB guest RAM, 1.5 GiB JIT and 2752x2064 Retina.
+Indexed invalidation is active; CPU synchronization reports zero platform errors.
+By 377 guest seconds the code cache has reset six times, and host pipeline
+creation totals 1.13 seconds across 1490 builds. These are cumulative counters,
+not a controlled speed comparison or a diagnosis of every pause.
+
+The final freeze is a macOS panic, preceded by a four-byte user read at guest VA
+7d04000f00 translated to unmapped PA ffffffffcf00, PC 181002324. The guest raises
+ESR 92000010 (data abort), with remotemanagementd as current task. This does not
+prove a Safari, Roblox or GPU fault. Do not suppress the abort or return fabricated
+memory. New rare-path logs compare the cached translation with a fresh page walk,
+including translation-control registers, to distinguish stale state from the
+current page table. There is no claimed panic fix without reproduction.
+
+A worker-confined cache reuses successfully loaded Metal libraries by exact
+binary bytes. It has strict limits of 32 entries and 8 MiB of retained binary
+keys (driver-owned library memory is additional), FIFO eviction, no failed entry
+retention and no persistence. Users of an evicted library retain their own
+functions and pipeline resources. The cache is local to one Metal device/VM.
+New gpu-libraries counters report hits/loads/retained keys and driver load time.
+HV_GPU_LIBRARY_CACHE_OFF disables reuse for comparison. It does not cache mutable
+resources, guest function references, serialized descriptors or completion stamps.
+
+GPU-backed tests exercise exact-key reuse with a real library, mutable caller
+keys, entry/byte limits, eviction, oversized bypass, failure retry and retention
+of functions after eviction. Existing native pixel and CPU tests still run.
+Hardware benefit depends on observed duplicate library loads; no large speedup
+is established by the correctness test.
+
+A reversible preset for 16 GiB iPads selects four CPUs, 8 GiB guest RAM and the
+existing 1600x1200 performance screen on this M4. It requires explicit selection,
+then a guest restart, and preserves the disk and JIT capacity. CPU count is a
+shared preference, as before. This reduces pixels about 66% relative to this
+log's Retina resolution, not a claim of 66% faster execution. It trades display
+sharpness for less graphics work and leaves host memory headroom. The log does
+not establish physical memory pressure as the cause of the panic.
