+# Superblocks and latest-main integration
+
+Upstream reviewed/integrated: be027b492bac818a3bb0c76fc8bbdd7aee42cbd2.
+Prepared from e935545, preserving prior native Retina/colour/refresh, JIT/bootstrap,
+flow-controlled Link v2, saved Keychain pairing, native geometry, scrolling and
+DNS/MMU/allocator safety fixes. This does not establish a physical M4 speedup.
+
+## Superblocks
+
+The implementation only extends conditional fallthroughs within the same 16KB
+page and stops at a conditional exit after 48 instructions. It preserves taken
+branch exits and dispatcher stop PCs. No arbitrary cross-page merging or guest
+instruction reordering was introduced. Larger code can increase JIT cache pressure.
+Default stays off. An explicit HV_SUPERBLOCKS=0 is now applied/logged when disabled,
+and machine initialization resets the knob when the environment is absent.
+Previously an enabled value could remain for a later initialization.
+
+Native regressions execute actual JIT programs with superblocks off/on, check
+B.cond/CBZ/CBNZ/TBZ/TBNZ and a reserved-register branch, page end, 48-instruction
+bound, stop PC, small-cache resets and an unset-option machine reinitialization.
+No claim that fewer block exits means lower measured power or faster compilation.
+
+## Main conflict resolutions
+
+* New bounded lingering-debugger detachment uses P_TRACED; keep-debugger override,
+  duplicate enable guards and existing acquisition/detach lifecycle remain.
+* Batched hot/cold instruction-cache maintenance and lighter B-to-B chain patch
+  maintenance integrated. Real invalidation repairs retain full synchronization.
+  Executable tests cover MAP_JIT and split RX/RW aliases. The lighter branch
+  maintenance is HV_JIT_RELAXED_BRANCH=1, disabled by default pending physical-core
+  validation; this self-hosted Mac is itself emulated. Batched hot/cold publication
+  retains the full final DSB/ISB sequence and is enabled. Existing index
+  and publication tests remain required.
+* Custom destination-page hash index retained instead of adding a competing RAM
+  page index. Exact physical target/collision tests retained.
+* Existing Metal trace gate retained. The lower-level command path now has a
+  synchronized cached trace query as well, avoiding per-command filesystem calls.
+* Upstream wait-state probes/phase stores require existing HV_WAIT_STATS=1. Host
+  thread rights are released during machine cleanup. Instruction-word profiler
+  mode 2 is ported into the existing unregistering, bounded-rate/session sampler;
+  diagnostic output is capped around 8MiB. Normal profiling remains off.
+* New 1/128 switch-flush checking applies only to explicitly enabled experimental
+  skipping; HV_SWITCH_FLUSH remains 0 by default. Do not claim it speeds defaults.
+* PR63 optional right/middle physical button mapping defaults off and retains
+  custom input gating and scrolling. Mapped held buttons are released correctly.
+* PR50 shutdown/restart, PR51 Rosetta, PR54 trackpad replacement and the updated
+  PR32 restricted-HID helper are not blindly merged. They require separate
+  lifecycle/input/signing validation and do not establish background execution.
+
+## Background verification
+
+Settings and boot logs report on-device background GPU availability separately
+from detection of the signed GPU entitlement. No entitlement is added merely to
+make a capability look enabled. The source app does not implement indefinite
+background VM execution. Until an authorized on-device task/graphics test passes,
+keep Henge visible while it hosts its own build runner. A positive capability
+report alone is not proof the whole emulated Mac can safely run in background.
+
+## Main display / viewer controls
+
+The iPad remains the emulation host and port 0; Duo remains an independent port 1.
+Three-finger tap hides/shows Duo controls without resizing the stream. Main
+selection is macOS System Settings > Displays > iPad > Use as > Main Display;
+it is a guest preference, not an automatic host-side video-feed swap. Existing
+windows can be dragged back; the Dock can follow the pointer between displays.
+
+Native CI validation and physical-device validation are reported separately in
+the build artifact. No simulator jobs, other apps or research benchmark builds
+are required for this IPA.
+
+The emulated self-hosted runner cannot establish physical instruction-cache behavior or AVE hardware codec behavior. Link hardware codec/pixel tests previously passed on physical-Mac run 42597605953; unchanged codec paths are compiled here but those hardware runtime tests are explicitly not revalidated. Protocol/credit/worker/discovery/TLS/Keychain checks and iOS UI type checking still run.
+
+Runner validation found the 1KiB tiny-cache fixture could not open a split alias
+(the attachment API requires at least 4KiB). The fixture now maps 4KiB, limits
+logical capacity to 1KiB across cache resets, asserts resets occurred and restores
+mapped capacity before cleanup. No production memory-mapping rule is weakened.
