+# Decoder backpressure correction — protocol 2
+
+## Evidence
+
+The supplied November 9 iPhone/iPad boot logs both identify custom build request
+`d549c36552f6c13bde16037ebaf9511e6aad1b81` and upstream
+`17e9ed9de5dd2aead31468c55ad4af0cd8df7a9b`.
+The iPad's previous-session counters show fastmem on, a 1536 MiB live JIT region,
+983 MiB used without capacity flushes, 1516 avoided duplicate placements and
+physical-page indexed invalidation. These confirm enabled paths, not measured
+FPS/energy savings. The current excerpt ends at listener startup, before a Link
+codec failure. No exact failed sequence is present in the provided logs.
+
+The reported error text maps directly to LinkDecodeWorker's old immediate
+three-job semaphore check. LinkEncoder released its own three slots after
+Network.framework contentProcessed. This callback means the local network stack
+accepted bytes, not that the remote decoder consumed them. Several TCP sends
+could therefore free producer slots and arrive together while the viewer's
+serial queue was still initializing/decoding. Increasing the receiver limit
+would hide the missing backpressure and grow latency/memory usage.
+
+The phone's 6140 MiB process limit is a separate OS limit. It does not establish
+memory exhaustion as the cause of this queue error. Fastmem off on a viewer
+without a guest VM is unrelated to hardware video decoding.
+
+## Changes
+
+* LinkFrameCredits retires each sequence exactly once, after BOTH successful
+  local send completion and decoder acknowledgement, in either callback order.
+* Sender GPU/capture slots remain owned through consumption. New remote captures
+  already skipped on congestion in protocol 1; their capacity is now end-to-end.
+  No already compressed reference frame is discarded to recover capacity.
+* LinkDecodeWorker frees its slot BEFORE notifying the sender. ACK handling
+  runs on transport/decoder queues, independent of main-thread presentation.
+* Queue capacity and decoder state belong to a connection generation. Cancelled
+  jobs cannot borrow slots from or acknowledge a subsequent connection.
+* Actual API/output callback decode errors are reported. Slow but successful
+  decoding is not itself a disconnect reason. Invalid over-window peers still
+  fail closed. Version 1 is rejected: update both devices.
+* Sparse logs distinguish successful decode consumption, queue delay, peak queue
+  depth and consumption roundtrip from physical presentation. No new timer or
+  per-frame log flood is added.
+
+Native viewport dimensions, codec clean aperture, quality/colour policy, refresh
+hints, primary Metal presenter, guest interrupts/completions, JIT/signing and all
+engine efficiency code are retained. This patch does not claim lossless remote
+video, guaranteed remote 120 FPS, direct USB-C transport or lower measured heat.
+
+## Validation
+
+`bash tools/link/check.sh` on an Apple-silicon Mac with Xcode runs:
+
+* Production credit ledger: local TCP completion alone cannot admit a fourth
+  frame, reversed ACK/send order, duplicates/future ACKs, concurrent callbacks,
+  failure, cancellation and late callbacks.
+* Production worker: a blocked old decode plus two queued jobs, stop/start,
+  three newly queued frames, stale-generation rejection and codec error handling.
+* Real TLS and hardware Metal/VideoToolbox path through LinkDecodeWorker, with a
+  deliberate 25 ms decoder delay, 36 frames per mode, three-frame blocked burst
+  and fourth-capture backpressure. Tests check native 320x240, 1920x1350 and
+  odd 2853x2007 output apertures, colour orientation, cursor and half-float policy.
+* Existing hostile protocol/TLS authentication, PVG port routing, graphics and
+  iOS deployment-target type checks.
+
+CI results are recorded in the build artifact's verification JSON and job log.
+The hardware codec tests run on the build Mac, not the user's iPhone. A physical
+Wi-Fi iPad→phone session, sustained decode performance and actual display frame
+timing remain unverified here. Install on both, connect before starting the VM,
+then inspect `decode-ack` on the iPad and `decode-consumed` on the phone alongside
+any remaining error. No macOS reinstall or Retina change is required.
