+# Latest main integration — 8 November 2026
+
+Upstream Henge main is pinned at `ba9392e7ce13c6e80f2a635cf4a10336f27c0964`,
+19 commits after the previous release-0.2 base. This includes the complete main
+history through that commit, rather than a selection of performance commits.
+
+Upstream changes retained include sparse whole-TLB clearing; targeted drops from
+switched-out TLB stashes; one-fence restoration of writable stash entries;
+ASID-plus-table-base branch-cache identities; TLB-first slow memory access;
+plain-register CASP acceleration; shared IOSurfaces for WebKit multi-plane tiles;
+installer memory caps and uncached restore writes; and larger automatic code-cache
+selection where the memory budget permits. New upstream experimental knobs keep
+their upstream defaults: no unmeasured switch-flush skipping is enabled here.
+
+All custom scroll, idle, diagnostics, optional kernel read-cache, security and
+PR14/31/32 integrations remain. Conflicts preserve upstream kernel-fill reset,
+write-descriptor selection and temporary-directory device tests while retaining
+custom chunking/EINTR handling and large-DMA regression coverage. Both normal and
+uncached disk write descriptors are covered by syscall-injection tests.
+
+The new single-page TLB-drop entry point also invalidates the optional read cache.
+The walker test covers both permission views and tagged addresses on this path;
+page-table edits invalidate translations before they are reused, matching the
+new upstream TLB-first slow-access behavior.
+
+Completed lifecycle work additionally limits periodic kick flags to observed
+active CPUs (explicit invalidation/device/stop broadcasts retain their existing
+paths), separates ticker waiter state from metric cache lines, and stops and
+disposes the CoreAudio output after CPU0 exits under the device lock. A late
+sound start cannot revive the stopped output. Tests exercise idempotence,
+reattachment, format changes and render pulls; native WFI tests also check active
+versus parked kick flags. These changes remove potential wasted work without a
+claim of measured power savings on the physical M4.
+
+The IPA records both its custom request commit and upstream main commit in
+Info.plist, startup logs and build-verification.json. Patch application is
+checked against the pinned upstream commit; native regressions precede IPA
+packaging. Local checks cover walker invalidation, disk faults, memory spans,
+duplicate publication, 490 emitted ARM64 memory cases and sanitizer-enabled
+idle/audio lifecycle tests. Native Mac engine and Swift checks run in CI.
+
+Native touch still requires authorized Mac signing for the virtual-HID
+entitlement and defaults off. This update does not solve that signing blocker.
+There is no cross-launch executable cache. Hardware launch-time, responsiveness
+and energy comparison still require a representative M4 run.
