+# Native Metal presentation revision
+
+The existing guest GPU replayer already uses native host Metal for render,
+compute, blits and direct CAMetalLayer presentation. No CPU-to-GPU emulation
+conversion or blanket removal of synchronization is appropriate.
+
+This revision compiles the display/cursor Metal shaders into the iOS default
+library. The presenter loads it instead of compiling Metal source on first
+presentation, with source compilation retained for command-line builds and
+missing libraries. A shared pipeline factory preserves BGRA output, half-float
+encoded/linear handling and premultiplied cursor blending. Completion failures
+are logged asynchronously. Normal frames still use the existing GPU texture
+mapping without CPU readback; diagnostic capture can explicitly read back.
+
+The new native-metal log reports device, library path and pipeline setup time.
+Precompiled shaders remove runtime source compilation, but GPU-specific pipeline
+creation still occurs. This does not change guest shader reconstruction or
+persist the CPU translation cache; it cannot promise instant guest startup.
+
+Validation: compiled/runtime source parity; native Mac GPU offscreen pixel tests
+for both libraries (four-colour BGRA orientation, RGBA16Float encoded and linear
+conversion, premultiplied cursor), then real iOS shader compilation and package
+inspection. Existing CPU/input/lifecycle tests remain. Physical M4 presentation,
+external-display changes and app workloads still require device validation.
