+# Native touch
+
+Native touch sends direct contact input to a macOS 27.2 or later guest.
+Trackpad mode is the default and the fallback when native touch is unavailable.
+
+## Setup
+
+1. In the guest, focus Terminal. Open Henge's Details panel and choose
+   **Touch input → Type the Helper Update Command**, then press Return in Terminal.
+2. Allow Accessibility for `henge-touch-agent` in the guest's System Settings.
+   The helper also requires authorization to create its virtual HID device.
+3. Enable **Native touch (experimental)** in Details, then close the panel.
+
+The setting is saved. Details shows connection and permission errors.
+Transport timeouts retry automatically after the guest helper connects.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+The virtual touchscreen binds to the guest's main display and supports up to
+five contacts. Coordinates follow the displayed image, including zoom.
+Contact transitions are queued, and movement with the same contacts is coalesced.
+Idle requests wait up to 250 ms; new input wakes them immediately.
+
+Opening a Henge panel, backgrounding the app, or changing image geometry releases
+the contacts. Missing heartbeats also release input and restore trackpad mode.
+An external display uses the phone's trackpad controls.
+When controls are hidden, a three-finger tap reveals them.
+
+## Development
+
+Build with Xcode 27.3 or newer. The iOS build bundles the guest touch helper.
+Run the focused checks from the repository root:
+
+```sh
+tools/check_native_touch.sh
+```
+
+These cover the transport, contact transitions, timeouts, reconnection, and Swift
+compilation. Hardware testing on an iPhone Duo covered direct touch on macOS 27.2
+and direct touch with the newer touch UI on macOS 27.3.
+
+## Custom iPad build integration
+
+Pinned PR #32 commit: `fd30cda9ffb6f93cefdd6ae67480c90d61f10334`.
+The native-touch negotiation task does not run when its toggle is off. The
+existing Guest sharing switch also gates helper access; enable sharing and fully
+reopen Henge before setup. Sharing disabled means no native-touch host endpoint.
+The guest companion, once installed, still uses long-poll requests/watchdogs;
+this feature is optional and should not be described as a general speed boost.
+
+The integration test now keeps helper heartbeats running until its simulated
+sender completes. Its original fixed three-poll loop could starve the watchdog
+while joining a slow sender. A deliberately delayed sender reproduces the old
+test failure; the corrected loop passes without changing production timeouts.
+
+## Confirmed signing limitation (8 November 2026)
+
+A stock macOS 27.2 guest rejected the bundled helper at process launch with AMFI
+error -424: "The file is adhoc signed but contains restricted entitlements."
+The Accessibility grant succeeded, but cannot authorize this signature. The
+virtual-HID entitlement requires Apple-authorized Mac signing/provisioning for
+normal enforcement. iLoader's iOS signature does not authorize a Mac executable.
+Reinstalling the guest does not fix this. Keep native touch off and use trackpad
+input while this requirement is unmet. The source remains integrated; no guest
+security policy changes or signing checks are bypassed by this build.
+
+CI now probes whether the helper reaches main without activating HID or opening
+network connections. Its result is recorded separately from compilation and
+transport tests, and does not certify guest HID authorization. This prevents a
+passing compile from being mistaken for successful guest launch.
