+# Pull-request review — 8 November 2026
+
+Reviewed the complete GitHub PR listing (19 entries, all states) and the diffs of
+all candidates not already integrated, against main ba9392e7 and custom 5353d6d.
+
+| PR | Decision | Reason |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 | Already upstream | Included by pinned main history; no duplicate application. |
+| 14 | Retained/adapted | Existing bounded raw scroll batching improves on original callback conversion. |
+| 27 | Existing custom CI retained | Current pipeline pins source/toolchain and verifies the IPA; proposed cache key lacks equivalent dependency/toolchain identity. |
+| 29 | Deferred | Closed broader JIT redesign overlaps open #46; avoid combining competing acquisition implementations. |
+| 31 | Retained/adapted | Real firmware capacities, bounded I/O chunks and EINTR handling retained with main's separate uncached write descriptor. |
+| 32 | Retained, default off | Source integrated; confirmed guest AMFI rejection remains. Compilation does not establish authorized virtual-HID signing. |
+| 33 | Deferred | Serial pointer queue sleeps 50ms before/after synthesized Control-click; movement is queued behind it. No queue backlog bound or session-generation cancellation is included. Needs an input lifecycle redesign and device tests. |
+| 35 | Added | Read the notified scene from documented userInfo key so pointer-lock logs are accurate. |
+| 36 | Adapted | Unique mkstemp disk files, immediately unlinked after opening; retain HV_TEST_WORK/TMPDIR and 384MiB large-DMA test coverage. |
+| 39 | Deferred | Useful installer-memory proposal, but no bundled byte-equivalence/fault tests. Changes IMG4 construction, ZIP streaming and USB upload together; final zero-length transfer status is ignored. Needs independent stream fixtures/error-path validation before adoption. Does not address desktop slowness. |
+| 46 | Added | Foreground task handles first appearance and delayed debugger attachment, with bounded polling and cancellation. Existing successful allocation remains cached. Does not implement general failed-allocation retry or persistent translated code. |
+
+## CPU synchronization change informed by the supplied device log
+
+HV_SYNC_WAIT=1 is now the iOS default: the existing upstream acknowledgement
+protocol briefly spins then uses a bounded kernel wait. It still processes the
+waiting CPU's own requests and checks acknowledgements/parked state. Unexpected
+kernel-wait errors yield the thread to avoid a tight error loop. Added cumulative
+wait/timeout/error counters identify actual use and platform failures. Setting
+HV_SYNC_WAIT=0 in henge-env.txt selects the original comparison mode.
+
+A native multithreaded regression exercises both modes: delayed acknowledgement,
+a parked target, an intentionally omitted notification, and processing own
+requests. It asserts the sleeping mode actually waits and times out, checks no
+unexpected kernel errors, and has a process timeout to detect hangs. Local
+syntax and existing walker/publication tests run before CI; native execution,
+Swift compilation and existing full IPA checks run on the Mac builder.
+
+This targets wasted spinning observed alongside 6-vCPU activity. A physical M4
+comparison must establish throughput, responsiveness and heat effects; enabling
+sleep can trade CPU use for wake latency. It does not preserve JIT translations
+between launches or fix cache-capacity resets. The four-vCPU comparison remains
+useful. No claim of globally optimal performance or certified PR safety is made.
+
+## Follow-up from four-CPU device log
+
+The four-CPU run is still build 5353d6d. It reports lower TLBI acknowledgement
+waits but four full code-cache resets by 162 seconds, code invalidations in the
+hundreds per second and later translation-lock waits reaching 43.3% of one CPU.
+This is not an identical-workload benchmark, and does not prove a single cause.
+
+Code inspection found hv_invalidate_code scanning every cross-page chained exit
+under tr_mu on each code-page invalidation. Replaced that global vector walk with
+physical-page hash buckets and intrusive next indices using the existing slot
+array. Additional bucket heads cost 256 KiB per machine; no per-slot allocation
+is added. Full cache resets clear the heads; generation checks and lock ordering
+are preserved, and collisions still compare exact physical page addresses.
+
+A sanitizer-enabled test executes the real insertion, invalidation and reset
+functions with platform patching helpers stubbed. With 100,000 links it examines
+201 entries for the target bucket, including a deliberately colliding page,
+rather than 100,000. Tests cover exact target selection, branch repair, duplicate
+insertion rejection, relinking and reset. Native JIT/MMU/memory/device tests
+complement this state test. New code-invalidation logs expose examined and
+removed counts. This demonstrates reduced scan work, not an M4 speedup percentage.
+The change does not prevent capacity flushes or persist compiled code.
