+# Thermal-efficiency engineering — 8 November 2026
+
+## Status and baselines
+
+Reference: clean upstream tag **0.2**, f9c12c93620af4c4c5f5f65f9793b72f883be682.
+Current upstream main: ba9392e7ce13c6e80f2a635cf4a10336f27c0964, confirmed from GitHub
+at the start of this investigation. Starting custom request: 4fd9a50600af2d33cadc729ba72f685c3777b56a;
+local immutable snapshot: 53c1ab5. These are distinct baselines, not interchangeable.
+The clean reference worktree was created from the tag rather than assuming an
+older working directory was pristine. Release, previous custom and candidate
+must be compared separately. Source hashes and function locations are in audit-index.json.
+
+Physical M4 hardware, Instruments connections and power measurement are unavailable
+in this execution environment. The user-provided a434cbdb run is evidence of
+serious thermal pressure and functioning Roblox, not a controlled baseline versus
+this candidate. No measured M4 temperature, wattage, FPS improvement or absence of
+regressions is claimed. Native ARM64 engine/GPU checks and source microbenchmarks
+are run by the device-build workflow before packaging; their output is retained.
+
+Retina/HiDPI, colour handling, shader output, refresh preference, brightness,
+vCPU count, guest settings, input and audio policies are not reduced. No Game Mode,
+sustained-execution entitlement, QoS downgrade, frame cap or experimental deadline/
+GPU-batch cache is enabled by default. Existing optional presentation controls
+from the prior custom build remain explicit opt-ins, off by default.
+
+## Findings, ranked changes, defaults and risk
+
+| Candidate | Decision/default | Mechanism, evidence and limits |
+|---|---|---|
+| Timer-only register updates | Implemented, on; `HV_TIMER_DIRECT=0` restores general tick | Previously six timer register types called the general tick; CPU0 also polled unrelated devices under their lock. New board callback updates both timer outputs immediately; normal device poll/wake paths and 1ms fallback remain. Dispatcher sees the refreshed deadline. Native register-dispatch and real guest IRQ tests, both callback modes, are required. M4 latency/power effect remains unverified. |
+| IOSurface allocation before reuse lookup | Implemented, on | Old path allocated and released an IOSurface even for a reused alias. Lookup now precedes creation. Exact identity includes all backing pages, first offset and full used plane layout; first-page-only aliases no longer count as identical. Native test requires 1001 aliases to invoke the factory once, verifies Metal texture pixels and retained ownership. No per-frame pixel equality inference is involved. |
+| JIT bounds and final tail | Implemented, on; `HV_JIT_TAIL=0` disables tail use | Failed fetch-add reservations previously advanced used beyond capacity. Bounds-checked CAS leaves failures unchanged and rejects overflow. Translator can reserve a smaller final chunk before full reset. Twelve-thread sanitizer test verifies no overlap, alignment, bounds, tail recovery and reset generation. Tail space is small relative to 1.5GiB: no major FPS improvement promised. CAS is only at chunk allocation, not per instruction. |
+| Idle homepage preview writes | Implemented, on | Serial utility queue skips only successful, unchanged preview captures; resets per VM session, retries failures and orders final capture before stop. Guest display frames are untouched. Swift concurrency test requires 1000 unchanged requests to create one write. Small auxiliary saving, not the primary gaming bottleneck. |
+| Guest CPU thread resources | Implemented, on | Previously unjoined CPU pthreads and malloc signal stacks remained allocated after thread exit. Threads without join owners are detached; attributes destroyed; signal stacks released on thread exit. No priority or CPU count change. iOS/Mac compilation and session lifecycle checks are required; repeated actual VM starts still need device validation. |
+| Duplicate JIT helper setup | Implemented, on | MainActor busy guards coalesce duplicate initial enable calls observed twice in supplied logs. Advised retries after attempt 1 remain allowed. Bootstrap mapping, debugger protocol and signing are unchanged. Swift app compilation is required; physical attach/detach remains a device check. |
+| iOS sampling profiler | Implemented, off unless `HV_PROF_IOS=1` | Bounded 1–1000Hz, default 100Hz, validated interval/duration, actual-time windows, Mach port lifetime protection, slot reuse, explicit unregister and condition waiting while stopped/expired. Stop waits for an in-flight sample before VM memory can change. Native lifecycle stress test is required. Profiler runs are not power runs. |
+| Secondary deadline kicks | Implemented experiment, **off**, `HV_DEADLINE_KICKS=1` | CPU0 keeps every original fallback poll. Secondary CPUs with an explicitly published future/no timer can avoid periodic forced dispatch exits. Unknown/expired states remain conservative; IRQ, TLBI, input, device completion and stop bypass the filter. Publication is atomic and only occurs when enabled. Native deadline and guest timer tests run; starvation/latency during real games unverified, so not a production default. Does not remove the host 1ms ticker. |
+| GPU batch lookup cache | Implemented experiment, **off**, `HV_GPU_BATCH_CACHE=1` | Sixty-four retained immutable function/pipeline entries keyed by exact task/ref/command epoch. Mutable textures/buffers are not memoized. Repeated backing-page checks within the same serialized command can also be avoided. Keys reset safely on epoch wrap and each command boundary. Production resolution-method fixture tests identity, collision, mutable fallback and disable path. Requires guest resource stability within a submitted command; physical guest workloads unverified. |
+| Frame, wakeup and WFE metrics | Implemented, opt-in | Presented timestamps yield host interval histograms (0.25ms bins, upper-bound P95/P99 and approximate 1%-tail FPS). Cursor/idle intervals are included; these are not game FPS. Own-task Mach wakeup counters report failure if unavailable. WFE accumulated ticks/timeouts measure time spent, not low-power residency. GPU timestamp accumulation and hot-path experimental resource counters are off by default. No invented GPU utilization, core affinity or watts. |
+| Local PPI arbitration and within-batch surface scans | Retained from prior custom build | Source microbenchmark compares clean 0.2, local PPI alone and paired local timer inputs independently. It measures host time and arbitration count, not energy or gaming FPS. Existing same-batch surface scan deduplication keeps resource synchronization at batch boundaries. |
+| Sampled IOSurface pixel hash | **Known inherited limitation**, not declared fixed | Real guest_hash samples 8 of each 64 bytes. Test reproduces an update at unsampled byte 9 with unchanged hash. It cannot prove pixel identity. Blind full copying can overwrite GPU-produced shared tiles; exact shadows add memory/bandwidth; universal dirty tracking must cover CPU, GPU, DMA and aliases. No new optimization uses this approximate content hash as an identity key. See remaining work below. |
+
+## Remaining bottlenecks and rejected shortcuts
+
+- The 1ms ticker remains for bounded device/timer service. A full event scheduler
+  requires auditing *every* completion/arrival wake and publishing timer changes,
+  then measuring long multi-vCPU game runs. The experimental filter is narrower;
+  it is not described as eliminating 1000 host wakeups/sec.
+- WFE may spend up to 50us in the host event-stream/monitor loop; WFI defaults to
+  zero optional spin. Changing those budgets can hurt IPC/locking latency. New
+  opt-in time accounting precedes policy changes. Hardware WFE residency and
+  efficiency-core/performance-core placement cannot be inferred from thread QoS.
+- Code-cache resets remain global. Keeping hot blocks requires reclaiming and
+  repairing all direct exits, indirect/return caches, literals, generations and
+  active CPU ownership. Larger cache or superblocks may increase memory/code
+  footprint. Neither is blindly enabled; 1GiB/1.5GiB require matched-device trials.
+- Full IOSurface dirty tracking remains unresolved. The reproduced sampled-hash
+  limitation is explicitly a validation gap for universal pixel fidelity, not a
+  GPU correctness pass. The new alias identity/registry change is independent of
+  that content detector and preserves GPU-owned pixels on a reused alias.
+- Guest command buffers cannot be merged or completion stamps returned early
+  merely to save calls. GPU waits/readbacks are retained when synchronization or
+  explicit diagnostics require them. Normal scanout already uses GPU textures.
+- Guest-selected load/store actions, formats, P3/sRGB interpretation, precision,
+  effects and antialiasing are retained. Presenter uses DontCare load + Store
+  for a full overwrite already; no unsupported tile assumptions are added.
+- Core affinity and thermal bypasses are not used. Guest threads stay user-
+  initiated on iOS; GPU submission/presentation stay interactive; audio's host
+  scheduling remains under CoreAudio. Existing utility preview/log work remains
+  utility. A lower QoS can worsen latency and cannot be called an energy saving.
+
+The original panic remains unresolved. Existing diagnostic-only fresh-page-walk
+logging is retained; legitimate aborts are never hidden or converted to zero data.
+
+See architecture.md, platform.md, device-protocol.md and validation.md. The build
+artifact includes the exact source/patch identity and native microbenchmark JSON.
