@@ -0,0 +1,109 @@
+# Reproducible physical M4 trials
+
+No device power/FPS A/B has been performed by this environment. The native Mac
+microbenchmark and supplied logs cannot fill those cells. This protocol is a
+required remaining validation, not an instruction to sacrifice fidelity.
+
+## Matched conditions and trial manifest
+
+Use clean release 0.2, the previous custom 4fd9a506, and this candidate as separate
+arms. Use the same signed identity; back up/export a VM before swapping builds.
+Do not delete the VM, reinstall macOS, change game settings or change resolution.
+Quit/reopen Henge between VM runs: the iOS bridge intentionally allows one VM
+per process. Restore any temporary henge-env.txt overrides after each experiment.
+Keep native Retina/HiDPI, selected 60/120Hz, brightness, CPU count, RAM and 1/1.5GiB
+JIT identical within every comparison. Do not apply a performance preset.
+
+Each run's JSON needs conditions:
+`device, os, guest_os, workload, scene, game_settings, resolution, hidpi,
+refresh_hz, cpus, guest_ram_mb, jit_mb, brightness, charging, case, orientation,
+ambient_c, start_thermal, warmup_seconds, measurement_seconds, instrumentation`.
+Also set `log` to the relative filename and record build/signing/tool versions,
+trial order, battery charge range and externally measured observations with their
+source/scope (game HUD, host HUD, device power, process power impact).
+`tools/thermal/compare_runs.py before.json after.json --output result.json`
+rejects unmatched/missing conditions. It does not infer game FPS or watts from
+coarse frame counters. Native presentation and external game-FPS measurements
+must remain distinct. An unchanged log compared with itself is a parser test,
+not an efficiency benchmark.
+
+Cool each arm to the same starting state; alternate/randomize order and repeat
+at least three times. Do not compare a hot baseline to a cool candidate. Record
+charging, case, orientation, ambient temperature and brightness. Keep external
+apps, radio/audio accessories and display connections comparable.
+
+## Workloads and observation
+
+1. Idle desktop for ten minutes, with no pointer/animation changes; repeat with
+   ordinary Safari page navigation/scrolling and continuous audio.
+2. Cold boot/app load and a separate warmed-up app/level loading phase. Account
+   for disk/browser caches separately from RAM-only translated-code caches.
+3. Fixed CPU-intensive scene and fixed GPU-intensive Roblox/game scene with the
+   same camera, players/action/replay, resolution and settings. Menus alone are
+   insufficient. Run 30–60 minutes where possible; mark shorter trials.
+4. Verify controller/input response and audio underruns continuously. Test
+   external display attach, detach, resize, reconnect and 60/120Hz modes, as
+   available. Preserve colour-profile settings and compare captures pixel-wise.
+5. Repeat initial responsiveness and late steady-state performance separately.
+   Pause a trial on panic/hang; preserve the complete current-run logs. Previous
+   run sections are not current faults.
+
+## Tools, sources and validity
+
+Use device Time Profiler for CPU stacks and scheduling, Metal System Trace for
+queue stalls/overlap, Game Performance Overview/Metal HUD for frame behaviour,
+GPU capture/counters for render bandwidth/ALU/load-store details, and Power
+Profiler for supported CPU/GPU/display power impact. Record whether the reported
+power is an estimate/impact score, system-wide measurement or calibrated joules.
+Do not relabel a score as watts. Energy per correctly displayed frame needs an
+actual energy measurement and matching displayed-frame count/window; otherwise
+leave it unavailable. P/E residency and actual GPU-active utilization also remain
+unavailable unless measured by a suitable supported device tool.
+
+Collect game average FPS, 1%-low definition, raw frame times/P95/P99, CPU usage,
+wakeups, GPU time/frame and active utilization if available, translations/misses,
+full resets, memory pressure, power/energy if available, thermal transitions and
+input/audio latency. No regression is established by a missing metric.
+
+## Instrumented captures versus power trials
+
+`HV_FRAME_STATS=1` adds host drawable-presented intervals: average FPS, 0.25ms-bin
+upper-bound P95/P99 and estimated worst-1% FPS. Cursor and idle intervals are
+included, generation changes reset histograms, and overflow invalidates the tail
+estimate. A 1%-low game FPS result requires game-frame data, not these counters.
+`HV_TASK_STATS=1` asks the kernel for own-task wakeup counters; failure is reported.
+`HV_WAIT_STATS=1` adds accumulated WFE ticks/timeouts; it cannot show hardware
+low-power residency. `HV_GPU_TIMING=1` enables execution timestamp accumulation; it is off by default. GPU execution totals can overlap and do not imply
+GPU utilization or per-display-frame cost. Correlate all clocks/windows.
+
+For an opt-in CPU capture, set `HV_PROF_IOS=1`, `HV_PROF_IOS_HZ=100`,
+`HV_PROF_IOS_SECS=10`, `HV_PROF_IOS_DURATION=60`. Explicit rates 1–1000Hz are
+allowed. The sampler perturbs execution and is not a power-run setting. Start a
+new app session to configure it. Preserve the exact unstripped binary/source for
+tools/prof_symbolize.sh. This profiler covers registered guest CPU host threads,
+not every Metal/audio/network worker or every physical core. Instruments fills
+those gaps. Disable the sampler and detailed trace/HUD/counters for uninstrumented
+power trials, or keep identical instrumentation and label the overhead.
+
+## Independent feature comparisons and rollback
+
+- `HV_TIMER_DIRECT=0`: prior general tick on timer MSR; absent/1: timer-only path.
+- `HV_JIT_TAIL=0`: old chunk-size decision; absent/1: tail recovery. Bounds-safe
+  allocation stays fixed; unsafe overflow is not a useful rollback mode.
+- `HV_DEADLINE_KICKS=1`: experimental secondary timer filter; default off. It
+  additionally requires timer-only callback. Test short deadlines, masked timers,
+  WFI, TLBI storms, CPU_ON/OFF, network/input/audio/GPU completion and starvation.
+- `HV_GPU_BATCH_CACHE=1`: experimental immutable lookup/page-check cache; default
+  off. Compare counters/throughput, resize/destroy/recreate textures and processes,
+  context/mapping changes, and long high-action game sessions.
+- `HV_GPU_LIBRARY_CACHE_OFF=1`: prior no library reuse for an independent comparison.
+- Existing `HV_IDLE_TICKER=0` compares prior periodic all-CPU ticker behaviour.
+  Do not disable real interrupts or timer service for a benchmark.
+- Superblocks and 1GiB/1.5GiB code-cache settings require independent, matched
+  trials: larger/faster is not automatically more energy efficient.
+
+Do not combine unverified experiments into the first candidate trial. Normal
+candidate leaves all opt-in limits/experiments off and preserves existing visuals.
+For Game Mode use the separate metadata build, then iPadOS Game Overlay on/off if
+recognized. Sustained execution needs an authorizing profile and installation
+verification first; it may lower peaks and is not part of this default candidate.
