+# Validation and known limits
+
+## Local checks
+
+- `python3 tests/test_jit_allocation.py`: real allocator/chunk functions, ASan/UBSan,
+  twelve concurrent allocators, alignment, exhaustion, overflow, smaller-tail
+  placement and generation reset.
+- `python3 tests/test_chain_index.py`, `python3 tests/test_translation_race.py`:
+  existing publication/invalidation tests remain applicable.
+- `python3 tests/test_surface_sync.py`: existing exact-object per-batch dedup helper.
+- `python3 tests/test_surface_hash_limit.py`: reproduces the inherited detector's
+  unsampled-byte miss. Passing means the limitation was reproduced, **not fixed**.
+- `python3 tests/test_gaming_experiments.py`: authorization fixtures only; not an
+  Apple provisioning or installed-entitlement validation.
+- `python3 tests/test_thermal_compare.py`: comparison-condition gate and honest
+  unknown values for unavailable physical metrics.
+- Portable C frame histogram and epoch identity tests; source parity and diff checks.
+
+## Required Mac builder gates
+
+Workflow: .github/workflows/henge-ipa.yml in the Sideos5 build request. It selects
+Xcode 27.2 when installed, pins main/Husk/patch digests, uses exact dependency
+cache fingerprints and real device compilation; no simulator build is substituted.
+
+- Clean tag 0.2 JIT, memory and MMU regressions, retained baseline logs.
+- Same-compiler seven-round native GIC source microbenchmarks, alternating run
+  order: release 0.2, local PPI only, and paired local timer inputs. JSON contains
+  arbitration counts and elapsed/process CPU time. It is not M4 game FPS or power.
+- Native candidate engine regressions, real guest timer IRQ program, direct timer
+  callback and fallback modes; explicit deadline-filter state/interrupt tests.
+- Native GPU pixel tests for BGRA/orientation, encoded/linear half-float, cursor;
+  exact planar alias/layout identity, avoided IOSurface creation, Metal texture
+  view pixels and resource lifetime after registry removal; library reuse tests.
+- Production object-resolution method test with controlled metadata and factories:
+  independent tasks/commands, collisions, immutable hits, mutable texture fallback
+  and disabled mode. Does not substitute for real guest GPU workloads.
+- Actual dispatch scheduler regression for existing optional presentation controls.
+- Native profiler lifecycle/ports/duration/stop/restart test; Swift preview queue
+  tests, failed capture retry and final-write ordering.
+- iOS Swift/Objective-C/C/Metal compilation, bundled metallib verification, existing
+  helper packaging and the final IPA hashes/source identity.
+- Entitlement source files remain unchanged. Optional metadata does not establish
+  real Game Mode activation; sustained entitlements are not added to normal IPA.
+
+The workflow must pass candidate gates before exporting an IPA. Read the retained
+job log and microbenchmark JSON for actual outcomes, including failures. A future
+successful build is not evidence that this device never stutters or panics.
+
+## Hardware-only gaps
+
+No physical M4 Time Profiler/Power Profiler/Metal System Trace, 30–60 minute
+matched gaming trials, P/E-core distribution, real power/joules/temperature,
+external-display capture comparison, controller/audio latency A/B, real Apple
+provisioning verification or actual host Game Mode activation is available here.
+Those results remain unverified. User-supplied logs are uncontrolled observations;
+no heat-reduction percentage, current-FPS uplift or non-regression certification
+is fabricated. The prior guest panic and full IOSurface dirty-tracking limitation
+remain explicit open issues, and no unsafe memory/interrupt error is hidden.
+
+The iOS bridge permits one VM per app process. Thread resource cleanup improves
+retirement after exit; it does not assert that the old app leaked memory across
+process launches or add unsupported in-process VM restart functionality.
+
+## Validation failures retained
+
+The first native pass stopped in an allocator *test fixture*: Apple Clang rejects
+a GNU atomic builtin applied to a C11 _Atomic-qualified object. The fixture now
+uses plain storage accessed by atomic builtins and synchronized reads after joins.
+The allocator production function was unchanged by this repair. The second pass
+passed that stress test and the object/scheduler/Metal pixel gates, then stopped
+on an implicitly boxed multicharacter constant in the IOSurface test. That
+fixture now uses an explicitly unsigned FourCC value. These failed gates did not
+produce an installable candidate. An optional histogram overflow-bound issue
+was also corrected and covered with a deterministic test. Final successful
+checks and source microbenchmark results are in the retained workflow artifacts.
+
+A subsequent run exposed a pre-existing test timing assumption: a dispatch_after
+callback was required to arrive within a fixed 100ms sleep on the shared CI
+runner (observed draws=0, pending=1). The production scheduler was unchanged.
+The fixture now waits on an actual delivery semaphore with a bounded two-second
+CI timeout, retaining exact frame-count, no-extra-work and stale-generation
+assertions. This tests completion/cancellation, not physical-device frame latency.
+
+The first full iOS engine compile then found a missing sysreg.h declaration for
+hv_counter in the optional scheduler path. The header is now included explicitly;
+the native engine/GPU/profiler/preview gates and source microbenchmark had passed
+before this compiler failure. No installable candidate was exported by that run.
