+++ b/docs/upstream-efficiency-20261109.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Efficiency integration — 9 November 2026
+
+Pinned main: 17e9ed9de5dd2aead31468c55ad4af0cd8df7a9b. Starting custom source:
+8bae133, including the delivered Henge Link port identity and odd-native codec
+fixes. This is an implementation and correctness integration, not a measured
+claim of lower M4 temperature or higher gaming FPS.
+
+## Conflicts and implementation decisions
+
+| Area | Final implementation | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| Code invalidation | Keep custom physical-page hash buckets for chained exits; add upstream per-page VA notes and selective indirect-branch-cache drops. Preserve full reset for multiple aliases and overflow. | The two indexes remove different wasted work. Upstream's whole chained-exit vector scan would discard our earlier improvement. |
+| MMU | Integrate occupied-chunk range filtering, CPU-major write hints and complete walk-log sequence including publication/reuse and temporary-TTBR0 fixes. | Reduces unrelated scans and false sharing. A process switch or uncertain/overwritten log still forces the original safe request path. |
+| Experimental read LUT | Keep owner-only kernel-page invalidation and extend it to remote ranges. | The incoming range helper had no custom LUT invalidation. Returning owner-required preserves posted-TLBI acknowledgement semantics; new regression checks this. |
+| Exact page-end checks | Keep our exclusion of 16-byte accesses from the extra recheck; preserve enabled default for smaller accesses. | 16-byte accesses already have the exact guard. Re-emitting it wastes code-cache space. |
+| Metal | Retain the existing exact-byte library cache, pipeline handling, planar registry, native presenter and Link capture. | Upstream's compatibility relabelling loader conflicted with the exact library cache. Target iPadOS 27.2 already loads these libraries; the iOS 17-only rewriting feature is deferred. |
+| Input/JIT | Retain the working input queues, scroll controls, JIT helper/bootstrap and viewer guards. | The Control-click queue adds sleeps; the new discovery fallback needs local-device binding tests. They do not deliver the requested engine efficiency and are not blindly imported. |
+| UI/signing | Existing Retina, refresh, graphics, CPU/RAM, metadata experiments and entitlements preserved. No lighten command, new 30-Hz policy, Game Mode default or all-branch CI imported. | No quality, responsiveness or signing shortcut. Existing explicitly optional controls remain unchanged. |
+| Metadata | Free new per-page VA notes and existing write-hint allocation in machine cleanup. | Added metadata must not become an unbounded retained allocation. |
+
+## Hardened host DNS
+
+The new host-resolver path is enabled with HV_DNS_PROXY=1 (0 keeps libslirp).
+The original IP total-length copy could exceed the fixed frame member even
+when UDP's declared DNS length was small. Bound that complete copy before
+allocation and validate EDNS option length/trailing bytes. Failed or timed-out
+host resolution now hands the original packet to libslirp for this query too,
+instead of returning repeated SERVFAIL before global backoff. Invalid resolver
+FDs and poll failures exit instead of spinning. Backoff is atomic, without a
+worker writing the shared engine-knob array. NXDOMAIN and empty NODATA remain
+distinct; packet queues reject oversize input and handle allocation failure.
+No query names, pairing keys or guest content are added to logs. Normal DNS
+still uses the device's configured resolver; no third-party DNS service is added.
+A fresh network session resets backoff. The one-VM process lifecycle is retained.
+
+## Small safety PRs
+
+* PR60 49239793759786555bf914875fb2bdef7bf14c4a: descriptor identity before
+  truncating an image output, including hard/symbolic links. Invalid image input
+  also leaves an existing unrelated output intact.
+* PR61 c8ce5d04dede4c4e95f5f156d93149203bcd46e7: synchronous installer .checking
+  phase prevents duplicate attempts while Boot ROM preflight is suspended.
+  An error returns to a retryable state. No installed Mac or user disk is edited.
+
+## Evidence and rollback
+
+Local ASan/UBSan checks passed for production DNS parsing/replies/threads,
+A/AAAA and EDNS, malformed packet bounds, NXDOMAIN/NODATA, startup/processing/
+timeout failures, bad FD, saturation, atomic backoff and ten concurrent queries.
+Production walk-log tests cover overlap, intervening walks, tagging, process
+switches, ring reuse/overflow/wrap and disabled mode. Real fast-memory walker
+checks include the new remote-range owner requirement. Indexed chaining still
+examines 201 of 100,000 links in its regression; publication/JIT allocation and
+Metal source/surface checks pass. Image converter alias/round-trip tests pass.
+
+Native checks must additionally execute the ARM64 JIT/MMU/memory/device suites,
+posted page-drop/alias/stale-generation/overflow tests and the Swift installer
+preflight fixture. The full iOS app and existing Link codec/transport tests run
+in the same single IPA workflow; results accompany its final artifact. No
+simulator, research benchmark or separate baseline build is required.
+
+HV_IJC_PAGES=0 selects full code-triggered branch-cache reset; HV_WALK_LOG=0
+selects conservative remote-walk race handling; HV_DNS_PROXY=0 keeps libslirp.
+HV_SWITCH_FLUSH remains off unless explicitly requested. Feature policy is
+logged once as efficiency-v2; existing statistics add targeted-drop and walk
+counts without a new timer. Existing cache, input and DNS counters are retained.
+
+Measure equivalent cold/warm starts, Safari and gaming on the M4 to establish
+whether CPU work, heat, FPS and frame pacing improve. Native correctness passes
+are not physical energy measurements. No persistent on-disk translated-code
+cache, lower Retina resolution, FPS limit or background game-work delay is added.
